-Single-stage YOLO detectors combine rapid inference with explicit bounding-box localization \cite{redmon2016yolo}, making them attractive for industrial defect detection. YOLO-based approaches have been applied to steel defects and large stamped parts \cite{gao2024srnyolo,li2024yoloxsteel,dong2024snf}. For fabrics, existing designs mainly pursue lightweight architectures for efficient inference \cite{kang2024ayolov7,yang2024yolov4tinys}, adaptive or deformable feature extraction for irregular defects \cite{luo2023deformableyolo,zhang2025dghr,zhou2025dcfe}, and improved multi-scale fusion or attention for small and weak defects \cite{yue2022tiny,yu2024fayolo,chen2025yolov8,wang2025srseyolo,gao2026yolov8,xu2025yolodll}. Together, these studies demonstrate the suitability of YOLO-based detectors for fabric defect detection. However, these improvements mainly emphasize detector efficiency or general feature enhancement; the characteristic spatial forms of fabric defects, including horizontally elongated, vertically elongated, and localized hole-like patterns, warrant more targeted consideration.
+Single-stage YOLO detectors combine rapid inference with explicit bounding-box localization \cite{redmon2016yolo}, making them attractive for industrial defect detection. YOLO-based approaches have been applied to steel defects and large stamped parts \cite{gao2024srnyolo,li2024yoloxsteel,dong2024snf}. For fabrics, existing designs mainly pursue lightweight architectures for efficient inference \cite{kang2024ayolov7,yang2024yolov4tinys}, adaptive or deformable feature extraction for irregular defects \cite{luo2023deformableyolo,zhang2025dghr}, and improved multi-scale fusion or attention for small and weak defects \cite{yue2022tiny,yu2024fayolo,chen2025yolov8,wang2025srseyolo,gao2026yolov8,xu2025yolodll}. Together, these studies demonstrate the suitability of YOLO-based detectors for fabric defect detection. However, these improvements mainly emphasize detector efficiency or general feature enhancement; the characteristic spatial forms of fabric defects, including horizontally elongated, vertically elongated, and localized hole-like patterns, warrant more targeted consideration.
